IMPORT prelude

-- Banking Act 1970 (Singapore) -- the public-facing core: who may carry on banking business (s 4), the deposit-taking
-- prohibition (ss 4A, 4B), the word "bank" (s 5), banking secrecy (s 47 and the Third Schedule), credit-card issuing
-- (s 57), and the order in which a failed bank's depositors are paid (ss 61, 62).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 35 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository (s 2 by 9, s 40A by 5). SCOPED from
-- 404,000 characters to what a depositor, customer or would-be lender meets. Not encoded: capital and liquidity
-- requirements, shareholding controls, mergers, prohibited business and exposures, inspection and control powers, transfer
-- of business, merchant banks (Part 7B), the credit-card licensing regime beyond s 57(1) to (3), clearing, and offences
-- machinery.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Banking Act 1970 -- the public`

§§ `4A, 4B -- taking deposits`

-- s 4A(1): a person must not, "in the course of carrying on ... a deposit-taking business, accept in Singapore any deposit
-- from any person in Singapore", unless a bank, credit co-operative, finance company, merchant bank, or otherwise licensed
-- (4A(6)). (4): an individual -- $125,000 or 3 years; others $250,000. (7): "The fact that a deposit has been taken in
-- contravention ... does not affect any civil liability in respect of the deposit" -- the depositor can still recover it.
-- s 4B(4): a "deposit" is money paid on terms that it will be repaid, and which are "not referable to the provision of
-- property or services or to the giving of security"; (5) an advance payment for goods, a security deposit, or a deposit for
-- the return of property is referable to them. (6): not a deposit if paid by a bank, a licensed moneylender, a group company,
-- or "a close relative" of the recipient or of its director, controller or manager.
-- (7): a business is deposit-taking if deposits are lent on, or used to finance the business "to any material extent";
-- (8): but NOT if the person neither holds itself out as accepting deposits "on a day-to-day basis" nor does so.
--
-- A family loan is never a deposit. A business that borrows from the public once, without holding itself out as taking
-- deposits day to day, is not deposit-taking. A tenancy deposit or a pre-order payment is not a deposit at all.
DECLARE Payment HAS
    `repayable on demand or agreed terms` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an advance for goods or services, or a security deposit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid by a close relative, a group company, a bank or a licensed moneylender` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the payment` IS A Payment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment is a deposit` IF
        `the payment`'s `repayable on demand or agreed terms`
    AND NOT `the payment`'s `is an advance for goods or services, or a security deposit`
    AND NOT `the payment`'s `paid by a close relative, a group company, a bank or a licensed moneylender`

DECLARE Taker HAS
    `lends deposits on or uses them materially to finance the business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds itself out as accepting deposits day to day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `accepts deposits day to day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a bank, finance company, credit co-operative, merchant bank or otherwise licensed` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the taker` IS A Taker
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the business is deposit-taking` IF
        `the taker`'s `lends deposits on or uses them materially to finance the business`
    AND (    `the taker`'s `holds itself out as accepting deposits day to day`
         OR  `the taker`'s `accepts deposits day to day`)

GIVEN `the taker` IS A Taker, `the payment` IS A Payment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `accepting the payment is an offence under section 4A` IF
        `the payment is a deposit` `the payment`
    AND `the business is deposit-taking` `the taker`
    AND NOT `the taker`'s `is a bank, finance company, credit co-operative, merchant bank or otherwise licensed`

GIVEN `the deposit was taken unlawfully` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the depositor can still recover the deposit` IF
    TRUE

§§ `5 -- the word "bank"`

-- s 5(1): a person other than a bank must not, without MAS's consent, use "the word 'bank' or any of its derivatives IN ANY
-- LANGUAGE" in its business name or represent that it transacts banking business. (2): exceptions include (e) a person that
-- transacts no banking or financial business, if the word is used "together with any other word to indicate ... that the
-- person ... is not a bank in Singapore" -- a food bank, a blood bank. (3): $12,500 or 12 months; others $25,000.
DECLARE NameUse HAS
    `is a bank or has MAS consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `uses bank or a derivative in any language` IS A BOOLEAN
    `transacts no banking or financial business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `other words show it is not a bank` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the use` IS A NameUse
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the name contravenes section 5` IF
        `the use`'s `uses bank or a derivative in any language`
    AND NOT `the use`'s `is a bank or has MAS consent`
    AND NOT (    `the use`'s `transacts no banking or financial business`
             AND `the use`'s `other words show it is not a bank`)

§§ `47 and the Third Schedule -- banking secrecy`

-- s 47(1): "Customer information must not, in any way, be disclosed by a bank in Singapore or any of its officers to any
-- other person except as expressly provided in this Act." (6): an individual -- $125,000 or 3 YEARS; others $250,000.
-- (5): a recipient under Part 2 of the Third Schedule must not pass it on. (8): a bank may agree to MORE confidentiality.
-- Third Schedule Part 1, among others: (1) disclosure "permitted IN WRITING by the customer or, if ... deceased, his or her
-- appointed personal representative"; (2) for a probate or administration application, to any person the bank in good
-- faith believes entitled to the grant; (3) the customer's bankruptcy or winding up; (4) proceedings between the bank and
-- the customer or surety, or interpleader; (5) a specified police or public officer's investigation or prosecution, or a
-- complaint or report; (6) an enforcement order attaching the account; (7) a High Court order under the Evidence Act; (9)
-- MAS; (10) a maintenance enforcement order.
--
-- Consent must be IN WRITING. A spouse, a child, or a police officer without a specified-law request has no route in.
-- After death, the personal representative -- not the next of kin -- consents, though item 2 lets the bank disclose to
-- whoever it in good faith believes will get the grant.
DECLARE Recipient IS ONE OF
    `the customer's spouse, without written consent`
    `anyone, with the customer's written consent`
    `anyone, with the customer's oral consent`
    `a person the bank believes entitled to probate`
    `the police under a specified written law`
    `a creditor under an attachment order served on the bank`
    `a court ordering disclosure under the Evidence Act`
    `the Monetary Authority of Singapore`
    `a journalist`

GIVEN `the recipient` IS A Recipient
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bank may disclose customer information` IF
    CONSIDER `the recipient`
    WHEN `the customer's spouse, without written consent` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `anyone, with the customer's oral consent` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a journalist` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- In months, for an individual.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment for a secrecy breach` MEANS 36

§§ `57 -- credit cards`

-- s 57(1): a person in the business of issuing credit or charge cards must not accept in Singapore any application unless a
-- licensee. (2): no one may accept applications for an unlicensed issuer. (3): no advertising to the Singapore public for a
-- card from an unlicensed issuer.
GIVEN `the issuer is licensed or exempt` IS A BOOLEAN, `accepts or promotes applications in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the card business contravenes section 57` IF
    `accepts or promotes applications in Singapore` AND NOT `the issuer is licensed or exempt`

§§ `61, 62 -- who is paid first when a bank fails`

-- s 61(2): the listed liabilities rank ahead of all other unsecured liabilities except IRDA preferential debts.
-- s 62(1), in order: "(a) FIRSTLY, any PREMIUM CONTRIBUTIONS due and payable by the bank under the Deposit Insurance ...
-- Act 2011; (b) secondly, liabilities ... in respect of INSURED DEPOSITS, up to the amount of compensation paid or payable
-- out of the DI Fund ...; (c) thirdly, deposit liabilities with non-bank customers ... in SINGAPORE DOLLARS ...; (d)
-- fourthly, deposit liabilities with non-bank customers other than [those]" -- FOREIGN-CURRENCY deposits; "(e) fifthly"
-- a resolution fund's claim. (2): equal within a class, abating proportionately.
--
-- The deposit-insurance scheme's own unpaid premiums come before any depositor. Uninsured Singapore-dollar balances come
-- before any foreign-currency balance, whatever their size.
DECLARE Claim IS ONE OF
    `deposit insurance premiums owed by the bank`
    `insured deposits up to the compensation`
    `uninsured Singapore-dollar deposits`
    `foreign-currency deposits`
    `a resolution fund's claim`
    `an ordinary unsecured creditor`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rank` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `deposit insurance premiums owed by the bank` THEN 1
    WHEN `insured deposits up to the compensation` THEN 2
    WHEN `uninsured Singapore-dollar deposits` THEN 3
    WHEN `foreign-currency deposits` THEN 4
    WHEN `a resolution fund's claim` THEN 5
    WHEN `an ordinary unsecured creditor` THEN 6

GIVEN `first` IS A Claim, `second` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first is paid before the second` IF
    `the rank` `first` LESS THAN `the rank` `second`

-- Within one class, a shortfall abates proportionately.
GIVEN `my claim` IS A NUMBER, `class total` IS A NUMBER, `assets available to the class` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my payout` MEANS
    IF `assets available to the class` AT LEAST `class total`
    THEN `my claim`
    ELSE `my claim` TIMES `assets available to the class` DIVIDED BY `class total`
